<p>Demonstrators joined a third nationwide round of &quot;No Kings&quot; protests across the United States on March 28, while related rallies were also reported in Europe, as opponents of President Donald Trump challenged his administration&#x27;s policies. Organizers said more than 3,000 events were planned across all 50 states. Guardian coverage said demonstrations were also taking place in 16 countries, with Minnesota hosting a flagship rally in St. Paul and other large gatherings in Washington, New York, and Los Angeles. Several outlets cited organizer estimates of at least 8 million participants, while Euronews reported expectations that turnout could top 9 million. The cited coverage said those figures had not been independently verified.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/oDw-_21e8ipvTqG-FsXLBHejetw8dr5lgeo5_RjTwkKxKwuk2ycQi9vfaZ7TBwvG6hpYfJMhrvEFHpEMWLsdj10d3f-kav8nRF1OTTFJ9yxQ7Xp5YyhOcEQGPqP8EKy0JVI1nX_KtMHd4jULTqVezCWGLhFt6-NV7aczmhMPywFoU0W1lKvyetoPLoa5IOVY3fTt-ny3RoRaFJ6coJlObks0TbTXYFcWkXWFrIgnD73056BBINvUjLlQMCemTTBl0Gv4A4Tcv12UhOssdw' alt='Demonstrators participate in a &quot;No Kings&quot; protest as part of nationwide demonstrations against U.S. President Donald Trump&#x27;s administration policies, in Washington, D.C., U.S., March 28, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Small-town spread: Two-thirds of the events took place outside major city centers, and organizers said turnout rose sharply in smaller communities compared with the movement&#x27;s first mobilization last June.</li><li>Minnesota context: Organizers chose St. Paul for the flagship rally in a state that had become a flashpoint over President Trump&#x27;s immigration crackdown and federal agents&#x27; incursions into Democratic-led urban centers.</li><li>Election-year organizing: With midterm elections later in 2026, organizers said they had seen a surge of people setting up local anti-Trump events.</li><li>Protest growth: The Crowd Counting Consortium recorded more than 10,700 US protests in 2025, up 133% from 4,588 at the same point in 2017, according to Guardian reporting on the dataset.</li></ul><blockquote>The rallies are a place for everybody to come and exercise their rights as Americans in a patriotic and safe way - Ezra Levin</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Organizers on scale: Indivisible co-founder Ezra Levin said before the demonstrations that March 28 could be &quot;the biggest protest in American history.&quot; (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/mar/28/no-kings-protests-trump'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>White House: Spokeswoman Abigail Jackson dismissed the protests as driven by &quot;leftist funding networks,&quot; pushing back on claims that the administration is undermining democracy. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/no-kings-protests-trump-critics-rally-across-the-us/a-76580489'>DW</a>)</li><li>Participants focused on Iran war: Multiple reports said many demonstrators tied their opposition to President Trump to US military action in Iran. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/0c214d44-1cff-42b7-ba87-54e717a1fccd'>Financial Times</a>)</li><li>International demonstrators: Protesters in places such as Paris framed the marches as opposition to authoritarianism and what Euronews described as concerns about &quot;endless wars.&quot; (<a href='http://www.euronews.com/video/2026/03/28/france-hosts-no-kings-march-as-anti-trump-protests-spread'>Euronews</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/no-kings-protests-trump-critics-rally-across-the-us/a-76580489'>&#x27;No Kings&#x27; protests — Trump critics rally across the US</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/gallery/2026/3/28/photos-no-kings-protests-erupt-across-the-us-with-a-minnesota-focus'>‘No Kings’ protests erupt across the US, with a Minnesota focus</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/millions-join-no-kings-protests-in-us-europe-over-iran-war-president-donald-trump-poli